    "teach_7": {
      "id": "teach_7",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Two long objects can hide both train length and speed, but subtraction still wins.\n\nA train crosses a 120 m platform in 18 s and a 300 m platform in 30 s.\nExtra 180 m takes 12 s, so speed = 15 m/s.\nTrain length = 18 × 15 − 120 = 150 m.",
