      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Capstone: three observations can form a chain. A train crosses a pole in 10 s and a 240 m platform in 22 s.\n\nExtra 240 m in 12 s gives speed 20 m/s. So train length = 200 m.\nIf it crosses a stationary train in 28 s, total distance is 560 m, leaving 360 m for the other train.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
